(A1 — global dynamic buffer byte-set growth inside a function must keep
 the reallocated pointer in the global BSS mirror so a later direct use
 of the variable sees the grown capacity.)

a buffer called b is "x".

To 'grow'.
  Set byte 10000 of b to 'A'.


To 'check'.
  If b's capacity is greater than 4096, print "grown". Otherwise, print "not grown".


'grow'.
'check'.
